WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.737
Deduplication has two separate problems.

00:00:02.737 --> 00:00:07.007
First, detect which rows appear to represent the same entity.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:12.502
Second, decide which row should survive or how the records should be merged.

00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:15.917
Do not jump directly from detection to deletion.

00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:19.887
The duplicate key and survivor rule both need to be explicit.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:24.892
Duplicate resolution requires a definition of identity and a survivor rule.

00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:30.142
Exact duplicate rows are easy; duplicate people or customers are harder.

00:00:30.142 --> 00:00:37.737
If you choose one survivor, document the priority—latest update, verified source, highest completeness,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:42.160
or another defensible rule—and preserve links to the merged records.
